     "text": "```json\n{\"reachable\": false, \"rationale\": \"Every exfiltration technique (exfiltrate_db, exfiltrate_fileserver, exfiltrate_backup) needs admin on db, fileserver or backup. Each of those needs a foothold there, and every foothold (auth_db, auth_fileserver, auth_backup) requires stolen_dbadmin. Only dump_dbadmin_dc and dump_dbadmin_adfs grant stolen_dbadmin, and they require admin_dc or admin_adfs. Those in turn require foothold_dc or foothold_adfs, which only auth_dc and auth_adfs provide. Both require NOT mfa_admin, but mfa:admin is deployed, so both are blocked. The attacker can still reach the internal network, the appservers and stolen_admin (via phishing, pivoting and kerberoasting), but no technique leads to stolen_dbadmin. Exfiltration is therefore unreachable.\"}\n```"
    }
